# CHANGELOG

LEGEND:
Development version <VERSION x.x.x> - <DATE> yyyy-mm-dd - Specifies latest version, not current changes in this codebase. use UNRELEASED for the date if that is the case

Development version Alpha 0.0.1 - 2026-04-13
-----------------------------------------------
- Deployed raw framework without game with a few additions such as the save and load systems.
- Implemented save/load system and forced username creation. Username creation does not cause any network effects, it's purely metadata, but useful for all kinds of games.

Development version Alpha 0.0.1a - 2026-05-03
------------------------------------------------
- Updated helper.py with some instructions on the asset string system
- Updated config.py to be neutral when using setup
- Ensured core systems were up to snuff # they weren't

Development version Alpha 0.1.0 - 2026-06-24 
-------------------------------------------------
- Removed custom surface object to rely solely on pygame's main surface. 
- Included unused experimental files
- Added more pygame wrappers in Window.py 
- Added a mesh loader
- Added a Triangle class
- Added a basic 3D math module
- Application name is now in a local config file (this is when the developer runs setup.py)
- Changed license to MIT. GPL just wasn't open enough for me.
===______=== removed unused deps

Development version Alpha 0.2.0 - 2026-07-07
-------------------------------------------------
- Removed most helper functions from helper.py
-- systems like reading and writing files are now in the save/load system exclusively
- Removed logging functions from helper.py. They are now in systemlogging.py
- Put time only on the system object and made sure everything obeys that rule
- Passed the system object to core systems (Window,AudioEngine,InputManager)
- Added network checks for all network related functions
- Added a Network class and consumed it with the system object
- Added a system telemetry.py in core/guts
-- This keeps values like the network connectivity and maybe one day CPU speed, and things like that
- Debug overlay now takes in values from dictionaries and displays them "key: value" on the next available space on the screen
- Refactored how game is initialized, added lifecycle beginning and end to Game Interface and its children
- Moved runtime inspector (game telemetry) handling to the Game Object, and deferred lifecycle to the GameInterface module
===______=== removed unused deps

Development version Alpha 0.3.0 - 2026-07-08
------------------------------------------------
- Upgraded network system.
- Added networking to core/applicatio
- Revamped UI and added a UI editor/Menu creator tool
- Renamed a ton of state systems in preparation for the Application State Tree Creator
- Added scrollable text with scrollbars
- Fixed window not resizing

Development version Alpha 0.4.0 - 2026-08-03
------------------------------------------------
- Renamed App to Runtime in core/guts/app.py, now core/guts/runtime.py
- Changed RUNTIME_STATE.LOADING to SPLASH to be more specific about what it is. Splash screens will be first class views
- Removed core/menus entirely
- Removed core/state/RuntimeLayer/Menu/*
- Majorly refactored entire UI system to be data based (JSON). UI elements now come from core/application/enginepersistence/menus and forms
- UIs can be hot reloaded and modified during runtime
- The contained application itself can be reloaded at any time.
- Established final boundary between the framework, the editor, and other applications developed using the framework + editor
- Updated build system to accomodate UI files for exported applications

Development version Alpha 0.5.0 - 2026-08-11
------------------------------------------------
- Textboxes no longer have a big fat border
- All UI elements using normals
- Added more customizability to multiple widgets
- Commands can now be openly registered anywhere to the command module. You can use the framework's key abstraction for keys
- Textboxes accept a max char count but by default it's 21
- Renamed core/guts to core/engine
- Renamed application_interface.py to distant_realms.py, moved to core/engine

Development version Alpha 0.6.0 - 2026-08-17
------------------------------------------------
- UI framework mostly stabilized
- Added install and run scripts for editor
- solidified setup
- Completed minimal documentation to use framework

Development version Alpha 0.7.0 - 2026-08-27
------------------------------------------------
- Added core/engine/backends with opengl and pygame
- Initilized pygame in backend
- Removed all imports for pygame outside of core/engine/backends/pygame.py and core/engine/input/keys.py
- Added Window backend config to config.py and example.config
- Added world system to engine. Migrated changes to Editor
- Editor will be a feature complete graphical editor for all parts of games now
- Removed application/ from core/. It is no longer part of the framework, but depends on it
- Designed a fully modular, reusable, configurable build system with built in deployment via sftp

Development version Alpha 0.7.1 - 2026-09-XX
------------------------------------------------
- Reworked the font system. Font sizes now scale dynamically with the window size.
- Updated UI widgets and debug tools to retrieve fonts through the centralized FontEngine.
- Font scaling now responds to window resize events.
